# subunit_sibling_call.z -- one implementation subunit naming its sibling by
# the bare name. A subunit sees its parent's chain, and the sibling is a member
# of the parent, so `wordops.double` written in totals.z is the file wordops.z
# this unit already loaded -- loaded once. A subunit's references fold back
# into its parent's load loop, and one naming a sibling already loaded parsed
# the sibling's file a second time: here both copies were emitted (a C
# redefinition), and under a system unit the copy no walk had reached was, every
# body in it bare (E0500 "unhandled callee") -- the uncalled member included.
main: function is {
    print "totals.sumDoubled 3 4 = \{totals.sumDoubled a: 3 b: 4}"
    print "wordops.double 5 = \{wordops.double x: 5}"
}
